# Same question as -11.play, retried: does RAID from home resume a live,
# still-*ongoing* boss pull after map -> back, or only a stuck/wiped one?
# -11.play (frost mage, idle) got caught by THE VIGIL's watchmen and landed in
# [[#3]]'s own retry-wipe stall before ever reaching an ongoing fight -- which
# did answer a *different* question (RAID from home resumed the stuck wipe
# screen directly rather than showing a fresh raid-setup screen, so the run
# is not silently dropped even in that state) but not this one.
#
# rogue:assassination has the highest flat moveSpeed in the roster
# (src/sim/classes.ts, already the explanation direction.md's #6 thread
# settled on for this class's repeated clean VIGIL crossings), under `good`
# rather than `idle` this time to actually engage the watchmen instead of
# risking another wipe-by-standing-still. 60s per room is short: Bonegrinder
# 10-normal has never finished this job's own reporting in under 84s under
# any style, so a live "ongoing" boss fight should still be running when
# evening hands back control.
open
tap raid
tap next
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
evening good 60 3
state
shot mid-evening

tap minimap
tap map
state
shot citadel-mid-fight

tap back
state
shot after-back

tap raid
state
shot after-raid-retap
targets
